    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d514-a2">

                <pb facs="0629" n="549" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg549"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blanco to Mr.
                            Russell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the<lb/>United States of
                                Venezuela</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-07-03"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">July 3, 1901</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On receiving your attentive note of the
                    26th of last month in regard to the entrance of the man-of-war <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mayflower</hi> into a port of the island of Margarita, I
                    informed the President of the Republic of its contents. The President took note
                    of all you had to say on the subject, and in addition expressed himself as being
                    much gratified at the prompt investigation made by you of this matter, which was
                    of the utmost importance as referring to the categorical provisions of a law of
                    Venezuela.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eduardo Blanco.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
